<title>LUXEMBOURG: Denmark sees no talk of EMU delay.</title>
<headline>Denmark sees no talk of EMU delay.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-06-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish Economy Minister Marianne Jelved ruled out on Sunday any talk of a delay in economic and monetary at a meeting of EU finance ministers in Luxembourg.</p>
<p>She also said it would be difficult and unnecessary to change the stability pact agreed in December at an EU summit in Dublin.</p>
<p>Asked whether there would be a discussion about a delay in economic and monetary union (EMU), Jelved said: &quot;It's not possible.&quot;</p>
</text>
